[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/k6/issues/comments/390301584","html_url":"https://github.com/grafana/k6/issues/636#issuecomment-390301584","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/k6/issues/636","id":390301584,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDMwMTU4NA==","user":{"login":"na--","id":3336773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzY3NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3336773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--","html_url":"https://github.com/na--","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-05-18T18:59:08Z","updated_at":"2018-05-18T18:59:08Z","body":"> Are the iterations in InfluxDB intended to match the number of iterations that actually ran? \r\n\r\nYes\r\n\r\n> I am curious if two iterations start at the same time, if k6 reports them to InfluxDB with the same timestamp, which means InfluxDB collapses them into a single data point:\r\n> https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v0.13/troubleshooting/frequently_encountered_issues/#writing-duplicate-points\r\n\r\nThis seems very likely. [Here](https://docs.influxdata.com/influxdb/v1.5/troubleshooting/frequently-asked-questions/#how-does-influxdb-handle-duplicate-points) is the latest influxdb documentation which says basically the same thing.\r\n\r\nCan you try running the same test (without sleep) but with the `iter` [system tag](https://docs.k6.io/docs/tags-and-groups#section-system-tags) enabled. Basically something like this:\r\n```\r\nk6 run noop.js --system-tags \"name,group,iter\" --out influxdb=http://localhost:8086/k67\r\n```\r\nIf that \"fixes\" it, then it's safe to assume that you've correctly diagnosed the issue.\r\n\r\n> Should k6 track when multiple iterations have the same timestamp, and in that case report a value higher than 1 to InfluxDB?\r\n\r\nI think that we should do that, so I'm tagging this a bug for now.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/k6/issues/comments/390301584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"na--","id":3336773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzY3NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3336773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--","html_url":"https://github.com/na--","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/na--/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":1634944946,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE2MzQ5NDQ5NDY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grafana/k6/issues/events/1634944946","actor":{"login":"na--","id":3336773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzY3NzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3336773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/